Subject: Bluetooth: btcentauri_t6050: implement native standard-header SCO

Target source: aurora-silicon/linux 8ab10100a4c1c944797e3fc8345589aff57777df
https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux/blob/8ab10100a4c1c944797e3fc8345589aff57777df/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri_t6050.c

Same-unit native 26C5035r inputs (private, not included in this patch):
- AirshipDK.framework/t2026-CentauriBeta.plist, 17902 bytes:
  b4b0736c3f2151b73d735d03fc1cfcfd1d52295954b6f9df7e0c464407766943
- usr/sbin/bluetoothd, 37723136 bytes, arm64e slice offset 12795904:
  eb0d4a8566365f95df5b6bc42537cef2cc1cec785834e507a55df9930c0dd539
- DriverKit dyld cache, 25591808 bytes:
  56fce56ce213e521e00cbfaa9e02ac0d9cd171b282a3f23fc7081c827f606b78
- Airship __TEXT, VM 0x2617e5000, 611944 bytes, macOS cache .52+0x13e5000:
  55b8f5a26b661dd04d4d035018a4c84feaaf1fa95b8733961d24c722e9232c29

The current native profile, not historical board inventory, selects in-place
TX3/RX9, nine slots, 724-byte footer, index vector and doorbell equal to ring
ID, main interrupt. bluetoothd 0x1000ee378/0x10015a174/0x100159fd4 proves
standard HCI SCO header+payload, then optional RX attributes: 0 terminator,
1 single-byte marker, 2 nine-byte marker/timestamp. TX descriptor length is
exactly three-byte HCI header+payload, with no extra terminator counted.
0x1001ac85c retains HCI packet status bits 13:12; attributes do not invent them.

Airship::tr_controller::sync 0x2617e9b30 and transfer_queue completion dispatch
0x261850d40 locate completion flags in descriptor byte 15 (bits 3:1), tag at
12 and length in word0 bits31:8. Tagged completion validation precedes SCO
slot reuse; errors stop transport and require a fresh firmware boot. Ring
ownership/space is distinct from HCI synchronous credits: HCI events and
core accounting stay unchanged. No synthetic completed-packet events.

Host regressions extract production functions, not a parallel protocol mock:
framing/attributes/truncation/status, wrap/full/unvalidated-tail race,
completion failure/tag/ownership, caller skb ownership, RX repost/ENOMEM,
command/ACL regression, close/flush/reopen/fault admission. No hardware run.

Private native HDR four-byte SCO headers and vendor HDR negotiation remain
unsupported. No foreign firmware, calibration, DMA/audio dump, runtime
installation or controller reset is part of this patch. Native reverse
engineering is source justification, not HFP microphone qualification.

